WEBVTT

00:00:05.628 --> 00:00:08.130
Revolutionary Calendar, year 228.

00:00:08.339 --> 00:00:10.633
It has been seven years
since Japan was invaded

00:00:10.841 --> 00:00:14.595
by the Holy Empire of Britannia
and renamed Area 11.

00:00:14.803 --> 00:00:18.641
To combat the spread of Britannian
power in western Eurasia,

00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:22.436
the United Republic of Europia
carried out commando raids

00:00:22.645 --> 00:00:25.606
with Alexanders piloted by Eleven youths.

00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:28.859
To secure the support of Gen. Smilas,

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:32.154
Leila Malcal traveled to General HQ
in Paris with Akito Hyuga,

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:37.034
but came under attack from Eleven
youths who lived in the Paris underground.

00:00:37.243 --> 00:00:40.955
However, their plan was foiled
by Akito singlehandedly.

00:00:41.163 --> 00:00:44.291
Leila promised to spare the lives
of Ryo and his two friends

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.504
on the condition that they
join her wZERO assault unit.

00:00:54.134 --> 00:01:00.766
"Euro Britannian Territory Saint
Petersburg Catherine Palace"

00:01:24.123 --> 00:01:27.209
In the name of the heavens,
the Earth, and the Holy Spirit,

00:01:27.418 --> 00:01:30.462
I, Duke Velaines, decree the following:

00:01:30.671 --> 00:01:35.509
That Shin Hyuga Shaing
be welcomed as commander

00:01:35.718 --> 00:01:37.803
of the Holy Order of Michael,

00:01:38.012 --> 00:01:43.475
one of the Four Great Orders that
protects the Empire of Euro Britannia.

00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:46.520
Lord Shaing, to me.

00:01:53.319 --> 00:01:55.779
All hail Britannia!

00:02:00.951 --> 00:02:02.453
I'm itching with excitement.

00:02:02.661 --> 00:02:03.787
Master Ashley?

00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:07.166
If I fight at Lord Shaing's side,
| can take the world.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:11.086
| want to see some action soon!

00:02:13.589 --> 00:02:18.802
The late Manfredi was a friend.
He would never take his own life.

00:02:19.011 --> 00:02:22.306
| know that better than anyone.

00:02:22.514 --> 00:02:25.434
| shall deal with the Ghost of Hannibal.

00:02:26.518 --> 00:02:32.441
My Order of Michael will restore
the honor of your Order of Raphael.

00:02:38.197 --> 00:02:40.032
Die.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.327
Akito, die.

00:02:43.535 --> 00:02:44.662
Die.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:45.746
No.

00:02:45.954 --> 00:02:46.997
Die.

00:02:47.206 --> 00:02:49.041
No.

00:02:55.756 --> 00:02:57.257
Die!

00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:53.939
This place has a silence to it that makes
the bustle of the city seem like a dream.

00:03:55.065 --> 00:03:59.361
Revolutionary Calendar, year 228,
Prairial the 7th.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:03.407
One month has passed
since we returned from Paris

00:04:03.615 --> 00:04:05.367
to Weiswolf Castle deep in the forest.

00:04:06.493 --> 00:04:10.164
| have yet to hear from General HQ
regarding mission plans.

00:04:10.372 --> 00:04:14.501
This peaceful time will not last long, I fear.

00:04:26.305 --> 00:04:29.808
Because I know that days of fighting
most certainly lie ahead.

00:04:35.606 --> 00:04:37.107
Akito...

00:04:55.209 --> 00:04:57.878
How are things progressing, Joe Wise?

00:04:58.086 --> 00:04:59.129
Without a hitch.

00:04:59.338 --> 00:05:03.842
The data transfer from the neuro device
should finish on schedule, Dr. Randle.

00:05:04.051 --> 00:05:06.261
Anna will be glad to hear it.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:07.638
Want a sucker?

00:05:07.846 --> 00:05:08.931
Not right now.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:10.474
Too bad, they're delicious.

00:05:10.682 --> 00:05:13.101
How do the EEGs of the other three look?

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.062
Promising, I think.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:19.316
They're kinda scary, but all three
have a AAA compatibility rating.

00:05:19.525 --> 00:05:23.362
It's amazing. They seem to be
a good match for Akito, too.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:26.031
BRS success probability?

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.242
Around 87%, I'd say.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:29.618
Really?

00:05:29.827 --> 00:05:33.372
Yeah, they're not even
parents or siblings. It's strange.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.291
You're right. It is strange.

00:05:39.336 --> 00:05:42.840
Hey, Ryo. How long do you
plan to stick around here?

00:05:43.048 --> 00:05:45.467
We get free room and board here.

00:05:45.676 --> 00:05:48.887
It looks like an old castle,
but it's high-tech and tidy inside.

00:05:49.096 --> 00:05:50.806
That's why there's not a rat to be seen.

00:05:51.014 --> 00:05:52.140
Right, Yukiya?

00:05:52.349 --> 00:05:55.686
That's right. Ayano, you hate rats, don't you?

00:05:55.894 --> 00:05:58.730
It's not like you to let somebody
put you into a uniform and do nothing!

00:05:58.939 --> 00:06:00.357
Don't get so worked up.

00:06:00.566 --> 00:06:05.112
| bet Ayano doesn't like that
they took her dagger from her.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:08.907
Damn right I don't! That bitch... or that guy.

00:06:09.116 --> 00:06:10.576
How could a Japanese be working for--

00:06:10.784 --> 00:06:13.745
Yukiya, have you finished
setting up our next game?

00:06:14.746 --> 00:06:16.415
Just about.

00:06:16.623 --> 00:06:18.208
What are you talking about?

00:06:18.417 --> 00:06:19.251
Tell me, Ryo!

00:06:19.459 --> 00:06:21.420
You don't need to know yet, Ayano.

00:06:21.628 --> 00:06:23.839
--Why are you freezing me out--
--Ayano.

00:06:24.047 --> 00:06:26.383
We're happy and content here.

00:06:26.592 --> 00:06:28.093
Understand?

00:06:29.511 --> 00:06:33.140
Are you sure it's a good idea
to keep those three Elevens--

00:06:33.348 --> 00:06:35.475
| mean, those Former Japanese
running loose, sir?

00:06:35.684 --> 00:06:38.103
Has there been a problem, Major Hammel?

00:06:38.312 --> 00:06:42.733
They're criminals who attempted
to abduct General Smilas.

00:06:42.941 --> 00:06:46.737
True, under normal circumstances,
they'd be felons looking at execution.

00:06:46.945 --> 00:06:49.865
Then we should let them
be brought to justice!

00:06:50.073 --> 00:06:53.160
Commander Malcal brought them here,
saying she wanted to use them.

00:06:53.368 --> 00:06:57.623
So why not? Gen. Smilas did okay it.

00:06:57.831 --> 00:07:00.876
If they take any hostile action,

00:07:01.084 --> 00:07:04.755
it will be difficult to subdue them
with just my special forces team.

00:07:04.963 --> 00:07:09.509
Don't worry so much. The security system
here is ridiculously elaborate.

00:07:09.718 --> 00:07:13.513
Besides, we need people like them here.

00:07:13.722 --> 00:07:16.892
People who won't be missed if they die.

00:07:21.146 --> 00:07:22.940
I'm sick of the simulators.

00:07:23.148 --> 00:07:26.735
They're comfy. They're better than
that other thing that spins you around.

00:07:26.944 --> 00:07:28.654
Yeah, you puked in that one, Ayano.

00:07:28.862 --> 00:07:31.114
I'm prone to motion sickness!

00:07:39.164 --> 00:07:40.666
A cat?

00:07:45.003 --> 00:07:46.797
Oh, I get it.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.595
May I offer my congratulations
on your son's success.

00:07:54.888 --> 00:07:57.307
The Shaing family's position is now secure.

00:07:57.516 --> 00:08:00.310
Thank you, Earl Orleans.

00:08:00.519 --> 00:08:03.271
We owe it all to the late Sir Manfredi.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.818
Come to think of it, where is
the party's guest of honor?

00:08:08.026 --> 00:08:11.530
Now that you mention it,
| haven't seen him for a while.

00:08:12.823 --> 00:08:15.534
--Alice, Mother is worried.
--Sister, wait!

00:08:15.742 --> 00:08:20.247
| hate these parties.
| don't know a single person at them.

00:08:20.455 --> 00:08:23.709
Brother, take me on a long drive
to the coast tomorrow.

00:08:23.917 --> 00:08:25.419
Please, Brother.

00:08:27.879 --> 00:08:29.798
Promise me, Brother.

00:08:31.341 --> 00:08:34.594
Tomorrow is the Order of Michael's
review ceremony.

00:08:34.803 --> 00:08:36.179
It is?

00:08:36.388 --> 00:08:38.849
| won't be able to return for some time.

00:08:39.057 --> 00:08:44.521
But I give my word that I will spend
my leave days with you, Alice.

00:08:46.189 --> 00:08:47.691
Wonderful!

00:09:07.085 --> 00:09:09.671
--Yes?
--Sorry for calling so late, Commander.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.214
| didn't wake you, did 1?

00:09:11.423 --> 00:09:12.883
No, I was up.

00:09:13.091 --> 00:09:18.013
Oh, you were? Operation orders
were just delivered from HQ.

00:09:18.221 --> 00:09:21.725
I'll bring them over right away.
You can unseal them there.

00:09:24.269 --> 00:09:26.772
Another damn suicide mis--

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.733
| mean, we've been tasked with another
difficult mission, Commander Malcal.

00:09:29.941 --> 00:09:32.736
This says that they're moving up
the Warsaw garrison force,

00:09:32.944 --> 00:09:35.113
but they're for internal matters.

00:09:35.322 --> 00:09:40.077
That latest public opinion poll must've rattled
the government bigwigs something fierce.

00:09:40.285 --> 00:09:43.080
If they keep the eyes of the
populace distracted outwards,

00:09:43.288 --> 00:09:46.208
they'll be able to cover their
own butts for the time being.

00:09:48.335 --> 00:09:52.214
Is that why they're having the
Wyvern Squad drop inside enemy lines?

00:09:52.422 --> 00:09:57.302
Well, to be blunt, they're to be decoys.
Or sacrificial pawns, I suppose.

00:09:57.511 --> 00:10:02.516
They don't have the manpower
they need to carry out the mission!

00:10:02.724 --> 00:10:05.602
You mean to say that you
can't simply disobey orders?

00:10:05.811 --> 00:10:10.023
You do know that sound reasoning
isn't going to help you, don't you?

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.695
| suppose you have no choice.

00:10:16.822 --> 00:10:20.117
If you really do want those Elevens
to come back in one piece,

00:10:20.325 --> 00:10:24.579
it's the commander's duty to think
of a way to make it happen.

00:10:50.814 --> 00:10:55.026
It. Hyuga. Thank you for agreeing to come.

00:10:55.235 --> 00:10:58.321
You ordered me to come, so I came.
There's no need for pleasantries.

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:02.909
Ah. Of course, you're right. Please take a seat.

00:11:03.118 --> 00:11:05.203
Would you like some tea?

00:11:05.412 --> 00:11:08.498
This tea has a lovely aroma.

00:11:11.418 --> 00:11:13.211
Is this about those three?

00:11:14.212 --> 00:11:20.093
Yes. I hoped to get your opinion
on the matter, Lieutenant.

00:11:20.302 --> 00:11:22.220
Be my guest.

00:11:22.429 --> 00:11:27.184
Do you believe they will continue to
behave and go into battle, Commander?

00:11:27.392 --> 00:11:29.394
| believe they have accepted their situation.

00:11:30.395 --> 00:11:34.441
That's what you want to see,
Commander. It isn't reality.

00:11:34.649 --> 00:11:38.278
They can't leave here and support themselves.

00:11:38.486 --> 00:11:42.073
Because they are criminals...
as well as Elevens?

00:11:42.282 --> 00:11:44.242
--I only meant--
--It's all right.

00:11:44.451 --> 00:11:49.623
Let's speak only the unvarnished truth.
| don't want to waste time.

00:11:49.831 --> 00:11:53.627
| expect that they also know what
you have in mind, Commander.

00:11:53.835 --> 00:11:58.757
In which case... you can be sure
that they will rebel against you.

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:55.272
| know about the drones.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:59.985
| admit that I prefer the idea of
using unmanned machines in combat.

00:13:00.193 --> 00:13:04.864
But I don't think that current Al can
live up to your expectations, Leila.

00:13:05.073 --> 00:13:08.285
They have to be able to react
instantly to their targets, right?

00:13:08.493 --> 00:13:11.579
Artificial intelligence like that
isn't technologically feasible now.

00:13:12.789 --> 00:13:16.459
Being in the military is a lot tougher
than I was expecting, right, Sgt. Hilda?

00:13:16.668 --> 00:13:20.880
| thought it would be a cushy
civil service job, Sgt. Chloe.

00:13:21.089 --> 00:13:23.049
Cause the boss is so enthusiastic.

00:13:23.258 --> 00:13:26.594
If we make a career of it, I wonder
if we can make Technical Officer?

00:13:29.723 --> 00:13:32.309
We cut the time down by 0.05 seconds!

00:13:32.517 --> 00:13:36.563
A new record! Looks like that
25D unit worked like a charm.

00:13:36.771 --> 00:13:39.357
Chloe, Hilda, is the upload complete yet?

00:13:39.566 --> 00:13:42.402
Yes, Boss! We're running the final checks now!

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:46.156
It's working really well.
It's all thanks to Akito's data.

00:13:46.364 --> 00:13:50.744
I'm glad to hear it. It looks like this
will let us roll out the Type 02.

00:13:53.455 --> 00:13:56.082
Ayano, what time is it?

00:13:56.291 --> 00:13:57.792
3:02.

00:14:00.045 --> 00:14:02.172
It's 3 already?

00:14:04.466 --> 00:14:06.217
Ryo, are you hungry?

00:14:06.426 --> 00:14:08.178
You're hopeless.

00:14:09.387 --> 00:14:12.390
Want to head down to the cafeteria, then?

00:14:12.599 --> 00:14:15.560
Nah, the snacks there are terrible.

00:14:15.769 --> 00:14:17.854
Then hold out until dinner.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:22.692
Yeah, I guess I'll try to
tough it out until dinner.

00:14:22.901 --> 00:14:26.738
It's for the best. We have
simulator training again later.

00:14:26.946 --> 00:14:28.698
If you eat like a pig, you'll puke.

00:14:28.907 --> 00:14:30.367
That's got it.

00:14:30.575 --> 00:14:31.868
We're clear.

00:14:32.077 --> 00:14:33.370
Attaboy, Yukiya!

00:14:33.578 --> 00:14:36.873
Okay, then... Let's get started!

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:39.793
Major Hammel.

00:14:40.001 --> 00:14:41.503
Anything unusual to report?

00:14:41.711 --> 00:14:44.130
Don't take your eyes off
the new Wyvern recruits.

00:14:44.339 --> 00:14:48.051
We know, sir. There's been nothing
new to report so far, though.

00:14:48.259 --> 00:14:50.762
They even keep that a secret?

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:56.935
You've always been a workaholic, Leila.
You need to unwind sometimes.

00:14:57.143 --> 00:15:00.563
We can't let this beautiful
garden go to waste, can we?

00:15:00.772 --> 00:15:03.274
This feels wonderful!

00:15:03.483 --> 00:15:05.902
Hm? Look at that, Leila.

00:15:06.111 --> 00:15:07.070
What is it, Anna?

00:15:07.278 --> 00:15:09.364
Up there. On the ledge.

00:15:09.572 --> 00:15:11.658
Isn't that Eliza?

00:15:13.201 --> 00:15:14.702
Eliza!

00:15:17.664 --> 00:15:20.375
| managed to hack into the server.

00:15:21.418 --> 00:15:25.713
The security camera keeps
showing us in this room.

00:15:25.922 --> 00:15:28.883
Also... I tweaked the data on these.

00:15:30.301 --> 00:15:33.805
| loaded them with fake data that
will let us pass through their security.

00:15:39.644 --> 00:15:42.355
How on earth did she get out of my room?

00:16:13.011 --> 00:16:14.637
There's a passage in here?

00:16:32.113 --> 00:16:35.366
Welcome back, Akito Hyuga.

00:16:37.869 --> 00:16:39.454
A handmade bomb, eh?

00:16:39.662 --> 00:16:41.206
Stop right there.

00:16:42.957 --> 00:16:46.628
Akito, you're too dangerous to live.

00:16:46.836 --> 00:16:49.839
So die with me here.

00:16:55.762 --> 00:16:58.014
What's the deal?

00:16:58.223 --> 00:17:00.141
There aren't any Knightmares in here!

00:17:04.687 --> 00:17:06.356
These are cockpits?

00:17:08.274 --> 00:17:10.318
They're down there, huh?

00:17:11.778 --> 00:17:16.324
You give off the same smell
as me, you know that?

00:17:16.533 --> 00:17:18.785
Let's have a chat before we die.

00:17:18.993 --> 00:17:22.038
Get it over with, or the
special forces squad will show up.

00:17:22.247 --> 00:17:27.001
They're not a problem. They're watching
a virtual reality I constructed.

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:29.879
But enough about them. Look at this.

00:17:31.839 --> 00:17:34.968
Look at this. Interesting, isn't it?

00:17:36.803 --> 00:17:41.057
| have lots of scars on my back, too.
How do you think I got them?

00:17:41.266 --> 00:17:42.267
| couldn't care less.

00:17:42.475 --> 00:17:43.476
Don't be like that!

00:17:43.685 --> 00:17:47.438
Have a little fun!
You're about to die, after all.

00:17:51.901 --> 00:17:53.987
You're a tough audience.

00:17:54.195 --> 00:17:57.657
Whatever, I'll throw it in free of charge.

00:17:59.117 --> 00:18:03.955
It was three years ago,
in Amsterdam's Japanese ghetto.

00:18:04.163 --> 00:18:09.127
The adults' sense of inferiority and
discontent had also infected the youth.

00:18:09.335 --> 00:18:12.964
They preyed on those weaker than them
to vent that dissatisfaction.

00:18:13.172 --> 00:18:16.050
Japanese persecuted other Japanese.

00:18:17.802 --> 00:18:21.973
The world was better off without them,
so I took care of them with a bomb.

00:18:25.268 --> 00:18:30.982
That's why I don't give a rat's ass
about Japanese. About Elevens.

00:18:34.277 --> 00:18:35.945
| escaped from the ghetto,

00:18:36.154 --> 00:18:40.158
and to avoid the police, I entered
the world of the underground.

00:18:42.285 --> 00:18:44.245
That's where I met Ryo and his group.

00:18:46.414 --> 00:18:49.459
For the first time,
| found friends that I could trust.

00:18:49.667 --> 00:18:51.919
| found a family.

00:18:53.338 --> 00:18:56.674
Which is why I won't let
any more of them die.

00:18:56.883 --> 00:18:59.927
I'm going to protect them.

00:19:01.721 --> 00:19:05.475
What makes you so sure that you
won't come back if you go into battle?

00:19:05.683 --> 00:19:07.018
| did.

00:19:07.226 --> 00:19:09.187
That's a real mystery. Some rumors say

00:19:09.395 --> 00:19:12.815
you used your squadmates as human shields.

00:19:13.024 --> 00:19:16.486
In that case, come with me.
Then you'll know for sure.

00:19:16.694 --> 00:19:19.697
There are three of you. And only one of me.

00:19:21.032 --> 00:19:23.159
| hadn't thought of that.

00:19:23.368 --> 00:19:24.869
That's true.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.586
Akito, you're an interesting guy.

00:19:39.717 --> 00:19:43.388
There aren't gonna be any communications
cables out here in the forest!

00:19:44.514 --> 00:19:46.015
Yukiya, you jerk!

00:19:47.642 --> 00:19:52.730
Are you returning to the castle?
What are the other two up to?

00:19:52.939 --> 00:19:54.982
I'm on your side!

00:19:55.191 --> 00:19:58.319
Give me a break! You're going to
use us as your disposable pawns!

00:19:58.528 --> 00:20:02.365
| am not! I've been thinking of a
way to ensure that you come back--

00:20:02.573 --> 00:20:05.910
That's crap! You're always
where it's nice and safe!

00:20:07.537 --> 00:20:09.163
How many have died so far?!

00:20:09.372 --> 00:20:12.041
How many Elevens have died
in your operations?!

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.711
| won't let anyone else die.

00:20:16.838 --> 00:20:19.340
I'm going into battle with you.

00:20:30.143 --> 00:20:31.686
Damn it!

00:20:37.316 --> 00:20:39.277
--Yes?
--Do you read me, Commander?

00:20:39.485 --> 00:20:40.862
It's It. Col. Warwick.

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:42.029
What is it?

00:20:42.238 --> 00:20:45.324
| see that you're on your way
to the launch site.

00:20:47.493 --> 00:20:49.036
Has anything happened with the Elevens?

00:20:49.245 --> 00:20:50.830
No, nothing.

00:20:51.038 --> 00:20:56.586
About that, ma'am. Our monitor feed
from their room just cut out all of a sudden.

00:20:56.794 --> 00:20:58.087
| know what caused it.

00:20:58.296 --> 00:20:59.756
You do, ma'am?

00:20:59.964 --> 00:21:02.884
I'll explain later. I need to hang up.

00:21:03.092 --> 00:21:04.635
Ma'am, w-wait--

00:21:23.696 --> 00:21:25.323
What the hell is that?

00:21:32.663 --> 00:21:34.165
Wait, this is a--

00:21:34.373 --> 00:21:38.252
An ultra-long range,
extra-atmospheric transport.

00:21:38.461 --> 00:21:41.297
We'll conduct commando raids
by using this new weapon

00:21:41.506 --> 00:21:44.342
to drop behind enemy lines.

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:47.970
Ah, I get it. Those are Knightmares?

00:21:49.013 --> 00:21:51.474
You expect us to fly off in those and die, huh?

00:21:51.682 --> 00:21:55.812
Since this is a war, returning alive
will never be a 100% certainty.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:59.023
Nevertheless, I'd like us all to return safely.

00:21:59.232 --> 00:22:02.652
"Us"? Are you saying
that you're coming along?

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:04.362
Yes.

00:22:12.245 --> 00:22:17.542
If you really mean that, you either
have a naive personality or are a fool.

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:20.336
As the one who proposed this operation,

00:22:20.545 --> 00:22:24.173
| intend to fulfill my obligation to ensure
that everyone comes home safely.

00:22:24.382 --> 00:22:27.218
| don't believe that to be foolish.

00:22:29.095 --> 00:22:31.264
Mark my words: You'll regret it.

00:22:54.662 --> 00:22:58.624
Sir Kururugi, we'll be arriving
in St. Petersburg in 12 hours.

00:22:58.833 --> 00:23:00.084
| see.

00:23:00.293 --> 00:23:02.628
How is the Military Advisor feeling?

00:23:02.837 --> 00:23:04.922
He's fine. You may go.

00:23:05.131 --> 00:23:06.632
Yes, my lord!

00:23:12.972 --> 00:23:17.393
Suzaku... Would you...

00:23:17.602 --> 00:23:19.896
Would you get me some water?

00:23:20.104 --> 00:23:22.940
I'm begging you... Get me water...

00:23:23.149 --> 00:23:25.192
Get me water...

00:23:25.401 --> 00:23:26.903
Water...

00:23:34.952 --> 00:23:38.080
82, 81, 480.

00:23:38.289 --> 00:23:42.919
Eight minutes to liftoff.
Launch countdown has begun.

00:23:43.127 --> 00:23:44.921
All systems nominal.

00:23:45.129 --> 00:23:48.841
Now, then... Let's see how far
the little lady can take this.

00:23:49.050 --> 00:23:51.761
Of course, if she comes back
in one piece, that's a success.

00:23:51.969 --> 00:23:55.598
Joe Wise, are you done
calibrating the BRS program yet?

00:23:55.806 --> 00:23:58.768
Just a little more.
I'll have it done before the launch.

00:23:58.976 --> 00:24:01.187
59, 58...

00:24:12.865 --> 00:24:16.535
Hilda, how much longer until
the Type 02 upload is complete?

00:24:16.744 --> 00:24:18.913
--45 seconds.
--That's cutting it close!

00:24:20.831 --> 00:24:24.335
All systems now switched over
from external to internal power.

00:25:02.248 --> 00:25:04.709
"United Republic of Europia Eastern
Front Forces Front Line Command"

00:25:04.709 --> 00:25:08.337
<i>"United Republic of Europia Eastern Front Forces Front Line Command"
An order's been issued for all forces 10 prepare for battle, eh?</i>

00:25:08.337 --> 00:25:08.546
"United Republic of Europia Eastern
Front Forces Front Line Command"

00:25:08.546 --> 00:25:11.090
"United Republic of Europia Eastern Front Forces Front Line Command™”
We begin our advance one hour after Apollo's Chariot launches.

00:25:11.090 --> 00:25:12.383
We begin our advance one hour
after Apollo's Chariot launches.

00:25:12.591 --> 00:25:16.554
Well, ours is but to carry out
the orders of Joint Staff HQ.

00:25:16.762 --> 00:25:19.056
Make sure not to go above and beyond
the letter of the orders.

00:25:19.265 --> 00:25:24.020
We shouldn't be made to take
the fall for it if the operation fails.

00:25:51.464 --> 00:25:57.762
This op, Operation Gamma, is to assist the
main EU force that's stationed in Warsaw.

00:25:57.970 --> 00:26:01.432
They will march on Area 24A
of the Eastern front.

00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:04.810
Our Wyvern Squad will drop
behind the Britannian forces

00:26:05.019 --> 00:26:08.355
that are deployed in that area
and conduct a commando raid.

00:26:08.564 --> 00:26:10.900
This will throw the enemy into disarray,

00:26:11.108 --> 00:26:14.153
and the 103rd Corps
will make a frontal attack.

00:26:14.361 --> 00:26:16.697
You expect us to drop
right into the enemy's lap?

00:26:16.906 --> 00:26:19.283
This certainly sounds
like an op that uses Elevens.

00:26:19.492 --> 00:26:21.410
Don't be so pessimistic.

00:26:21.619 --> 00:26:26.832
If you meet up with the advancing 103rd,
you'll come home safe.

00:26:27.041 --> 00:26:29.001
With enemy forces in all directions?

00:26:29.210 --> 00:26:31.253
We have to live that long first.

00:26:31.462 --> 00:26:35.758
You Former Japanese youngsters
sure are negative Nellies.

00:26:35.966 --> 00:26:40.763
All right, allow me to deliver
slightly happier news.

00:26:40.971 --> 00:26:44.100
The commander herself will
take part in this operation.

00:26:46.936 --> 00:26:48.270
Leila, are you serious?

00:26:48.479 --> 00:26:53.984
A commando raid will be ineffective
unless sufficient troops are committed.

00:26:54.193 --> 00:26:59.406
Unfortunately, we have only a handful
of personnel to allocate to this operation.

00:26:59.615 --> 00:27:04.703
To bolster those numbers,
I've decided to employ drones.

00:27:04.912 --> 00:27:09.625
However, an operator is needed
to control those drones.

00:27:09.834 --> 00:27:13.754
For that reason, I am going
to go into battle with you.

00:27:21.971 --> 00:27:24.014
That guy, he...!

00:27:24.223 --> 00:27:27.101
Ayano, you should catch some sleep.

00:27:27.309 --> 00:27:29.562
It's not like we'll have
anything to do for a while.

00:27:29.770 --> 00:27:34.650
You have a point. And if you're asleep,
you won't be afraid when you die.

00:27:39.572 --> 00:27:42.491
T-minus one minute to liftoff.
Activate drive batteries.

00:27:42.700 --> 00:27:44.243
Flight mode on.

00:27:44.451 --> 00:27:48.455
56, 55, 54, 53...

00:28:00.384 --> 00:28:06.265
10,9,8,7,6,5...

00:28:06.473 --> 00:28:08.475
All systems ready for launch!

00:28:08.684 --> 00:28:10.477
Main engine start!

00:28:49.516 --> 00:28:51.268
Go, baby, go...

00:28:51.477 --> 00:28:53.646
35, 36...

00:29:15.334 --> 00:29:18.003
78,79, 180...

00:29:18.212 --> 00:29:19.421
T-plus three minutes!

00:29:19.630 --> 00:29:21.215
Primary engine burn nominal.

00:29:21.423 --> 00:29:23.592
Control systems and flight path both nominal.

00:29:23.801 --> 00:29:27.096
Altitude, 108km. Velocity, 2.2km/s.

00:29:27.304 --> 00:29:30.099
Apollo's Chariot is
continuing to fly smoothly.

00:29:34.061 --> 00:29:35.938
Primary engine burn complete!

00:29:36.146 --> 00:29:37.690
Separate first stage rocket!

00:29:39.692 --> 00:29:41.527
First stage rocket separation successful.

00:29:41.735 --> 00:29:43.445
Secondary engine, begin burn!

00:29:46.198 --> 00:29:50.452
Altitude, 255km... Velocity, 5.6km/s...

00:29:54.999 --> 00:29:57.710
Apollo's Chariot,
secondary engine burn complete.

00:30:13.559 --> 00:30:15.436
Inertial guidance operating properly.

00:30:17.104 --> 00:30:19.440
Now here comes the hard part.

00:30:28.699 --> 00:30:31.285
This isn't too bad as last sights go.

00:30:31.493 --> 00:30:36.415
To think there are people down there...
| wish I could squash them.

00:30:36.623 --> 00:30:38.292
It's beautiful.

00:30:45.799 --> 00:30:47.009
God, I'm bored.

00:30:47.217 --> 00:30:50.554
Bored, bored...

00:30:50.763 --> 00:30:54.558
How long are we gonna have to stay
cooped up in the musty dump?!

00:30:54.767 --> 00:30:55.851
Joannes!

00:30:56.060 --> 00:30:58.479
Yes, Master Ashley!

00:31:04.693 --> 00:31:06.904
We have some time on our hands...

00:31:08.072 --> 00:31:09.907
...so let's play a little game.

00:31:11.033 --> 00:31:16.372
Joannes, to survive on the battlefield,
what is the one thing you have to have?

00:31:16.580 --> 00:31:19.166
Th-The skill to emerge victorious.

00:31:19.375 --> 00:31:21.752
What's with that lame answer?

00:31:24.463 --> 00:31:30.677
Listen closely. The absolutely crucial
thing on a battlefield is luck.

00:31:31.887 --> 00:31:36.100
Even with skill and effort, when you
happen to lose, you lose and you die.

00:31:36.308 --> 00:31:39.436
Why is that? It's because
you didn't have any luck.

00:31:39.645 --> 00:31:41.897
But I'm not like that.

00:31:42.106 --> 00:31:45.567
I'll show you the proof right now.

00:31:47.152 --> 00:31:50.072
Master Ashley! Please stop!

00:31:57.037 --> 00:31:59.373
See? I won't die.

00:31:59.581 --> 00:32:01.083
Pathetic.

00:32:03.335 --> 00:32:05.671
To think that you believe in luck.

00:32:05.879 --> 00:32:09.007
| wouldn't have pegged you
for a romantic, Ashley Ashra.

00:32:09.216 --> 00:32:10.926
Jean Rowe!

00:32:12.970 --> 00:32:19.351
Okay, then, I'm gonna check
to see if you have any luck!

00:32:22.813 --> 00:32:25.274
How about it? Feeling confident?

00:32:25.482 --> 00:32:27.693
This is bad. Private disputes
are punishable by death!

00:32:27.901 --> 00:32:30.487
--Please stop this, Master Ashley!
--Stay back!

00:32:30.696 --> 00:32:34.491
Stay where you are and watch!
See what Jean's luck is like.

00:32:50.340 --> 00:32:53.552
Looks like you have a pretty
healthy dose of luck yourself.

00:32:53.760 --> 00:32:55.971
That's enough of your stupid games.

00:32:56.180 --> 00:32:59.224
But I always get bored in places like this!

00:32:59.433 --> 00:33:02.144
In that case, you won't be bored for long.

00:33:02.352 --> 00:33:05.772
Lord Shaing wants to see you, Ashley Ashra.

00:33:08.192 --> 00:33:12.279
My Ashra Force is going into battle!

00:33:13.280 --> 00:33:14.907
Thirty seconds to fairing separation.

00:33:15.115 --> 00:33:17.784
This is gonna work... I hope.

00:33:17.993 --> 00:33:19.495
Leila...

00:33:24.291 --> 00:33:26.543
--System shows all clear!
--Commencing separation!

00:33:29.671 --> 00:33:33.008
Capsule separation confirmed.
System activation confirmed.

00:33:33.217 --> 00:33:34.551
All units show green.

00:33:34.760 --> 00:33:36.011
Finally...

00:33:36.220 --> 00:33:38.847
We're free falling
from 300 kilometers, Ayano!

00:33:39.056 --> 00:33:40.641
| know that!

00:33:40.849 --> 00:33:42.851
Twenty seconds to reentry!

00:33:43.894 --> 00:33:46.355
Ten seconds to capsule reentry!

00:34:10.629 --> 00:34:12.297
Wing deployment successful!

00:34:18.887 --> 00:34:21.306
Got it! This is a piece of cake!

00:34:24.768 --> 00:34:26.270
They opened!

00:34:27.271 --> 00:34:28.772
Did it!

00:35:03.974 --> 00:35:05.726
I'm being blown off course!

00:35:21.491 --> 00:35:23.660
Everything went smoothly in the simulation...

00:35:29.666 --> 00:35:31.251
All drones confirmed.

00:35:31.460 --> 00:35:36.256
Warrant Officers Sayama, Naruse,
and Kosaka, report your location.

00:35:43.180 --> 00:35:47.142
In a war, commanders sometimes
get killed first, you know?

00:35:53.607 --> 00:35:57.778
It. Hyuga! Make sure you
capture them unharmed!

00:35:57.986 --> 00:35:59.738
I'm not sure I can.

00:36:01.448 --> 00:36:03.742
Safe landing of all Wyverns confirmed!

00:36:03.950 --> 00:36:05.952
Beginning deploy-- Huh?

00:36:06.161 --> 00:36:08.497
They're already exchanging fire?

00:36:08.705 --> 00:36:10.457
Have they been spotted already?

00:36:10.666 --> 00:36:12.334
Isn't this friendly fire?

00:36:12.542 --> 00:36:14.711
It sure seems that way from this telemetry.

00:36:14.920 --> 00:36:17.506
Yukiya, target Hyuga from behind!

00:36:20.133 --> 00:36:23.637
It's kind of a waste to kill him here, isn't it?

00:36:25.597 --> 00:36:27.099
It. Hyuga!

00:36:30.060 --> 00:36:31.520
Yukiya, what are you doing?!

00:36:31.728 --> 00:36:33.522
Hurry!

00:36:33.730 --> 00:36:35.232
Fine, fine...

00:36:46.493 --> 00:36:49.246
What's all this? Could somebody
tell me what's going on?

00:36:49.454 --> 00:36:51.998
--It's probably enemy bombardment!
--Multiple heat sources!

00:36:52.207 --> 00:36:54.751
Shells impacting at the Wyverns' drop point!

00:36:54.960 --> 00:36:58.046
Seriously? Where's the fire coming from?

00:36:58.255 --> 00:37:01.341
Large-caliber cannons not detected!

00:37:01.550 --> 00:37:06.096
High-altitude observation balloon-- Data lost!
I've lost Wyvern Squad's coordinates!

00:37:06.304 --> 00:37:08.181
Can't you do a trajectory calculation?!

00:37:08.390 --> 00:37:11.852
Calculation complete! Five hundred
kilometers to the east-northeast!

00:37:12.060 --> 00:37:13.437
Five hundred kilometers?!

00:37:13.645 --> 00:37:16.064
Sara, are you sure you
ran those numbers right?

00:37:16.273 --> 00:37:18.650
I'm sure! They're correct!

00:37:18.859 --> 00:37:22.028
So they're using
ultra-long range cannons, huh?

00:37:22.237 --> 00:37:25.282
Our Britannian buddies had
a clever idea, too, didn't they?

00:37:52.517 --> 00:37:55.729
If we bear north-northwest,
we'll get clear of the impact zone.

00:38:07.199 --> 00:38:09.242
A Britannian Knightmare squad, huh?

00:38:33.517 --> 00:38:36.478
I'll settle things with you once
we've made it out of here alive!

00:38:36.686 --> 00:38:38.980
| wish you'd make up your mind.

00:38:42.567 --> 00:38:44.694
Ayano! Try to keep up!

00:38:54.746 --> 00:38:57.874
As you predicted, Lord Hyuga,
the Ghost of Hannibal

00:38:58.083 --> 00:39:00.001
are now headed towards Slonim.

00:39:01.211 --> 00:39:02.546
And Ashley and his team?

00:39:02.754 --> 00:39:05.882
In position, as per your orders.

00:39:06.091 --> 00:39:09.302
Jean, prepare my Vercingetorix.

00:39:09.511 --> 00:39:12.764
You're going to go into battle yourself, sir?

00:39:12.973 --> 00:39:16.059
| want to see who these ghosts
are with my own two eyes.

00:39:19.813 --> 00:39:24.192
"Euro Britannian Territory
Slonim"

00:39:39.499 --> 00:39:41.001
Why is it empty?

00:39:54.681 --> 00:39:57.851
This isn't good.
This place gives me the creeps.

00:39:58.059 --> 00:40:00.186
| think it's gonna be fun.

00:40:00.395 --> 00:40:03.815
Nothing good ever comes of it
when you say "fun," Yukiya.

00:40:12.991 --> 00:40:16.077
Drone deployment confirmed.
All that's left now is--

00:40:23.585 --> 00:40:24.794
An ambush?

00:40:25.003 --> 00:40:27.505
Commander, don't leave my side.

00:40:27.714 --> 00:40:28.965
It. Hyuga!

00:40:29.174 --> 00:40:33.094
We need to ensure that you don't die
before all your drones are used up.

00:40:34.054 --> 00:40:37.891
Understood. I'll do my best to make it
home alive with the rest of you.

00:40:47.025 --> 00:40:48.944
These are the Ghost of Hannibal?

00:40:50.320 --> 00:40:52.030
Uh-oh, it's the enemy!

00:41:00.830 --> 00:41:03.959
This is a... There are drones mixed
in with the Ghost of Hannibal!

00:41:04.167 --> 00:41:05.460
There's no sign of the enemy.

00:41:05.669 --> 00:41:07.379
They're close.

00:41:08.546 --> 00:41:10.048
Ayano, above you!

00:41:23.853 --> 00:41:27.482
Rene, Franz! I've located
the Ghost of Hannibal!

00:41:34.823 --> 00:41:38.076
Master Ashley! Most of the enemy
Knightmares are drones!

00:41:38.284 --> 00:41:41.997
The reality of the Ghost of Hannibal
doesn't live up to the hype.

00:41:42.205 --> 00:41:45.000
Enemy units heading
your way, Master Ashley!

00:41:45.208 --> 00:41:47.419
| was getting sick of waiting!

00:41:52.257 --> 00:41:54.843
Commander, can you call
the drones over here?

00:41:55.051 --> 00:41:59.055
The remaining three--two drones
are currently engaging the enemy.

00:41:59.264 --> 00:42:02.100
We'll force our way through, then.

00:42:02.308 --> 00:42:03.768
Stick close to me.

00:42:03.977 --> 00:42:05.478
It. Hyuga!

00:42:09.774 --> 00:42:11.359
Commander!

00:42:11.568 --> 00:42:14.195
Commander, get clear.

00:42:16.656 --> 00:42:18.199
A red Knightmare...

00:42:21.870 --> 00:42:25.248
Okay, let's get to killing!

00:42:38.511 --> 00:42:40.764
| see the other one!

00:42:47.228 --> 00:42:49.064
It. Hyuga...

00:42:49.272 --> 00:42:52.233
Die... Die...

00:42:52.442 --> 00:42:53.943
Die...

00:42:57.530 --> 00:42:59.032
Master Ashley!

00:43:00.325 --> 00:43:02.077
Die!

00:43:02.285 --> 00:43:03.453
What?

00:43:03.661 --> 00:43:04.913
What was that?!

00:43:05.121 --> 00:43:06.623
Akito?

00:43:07.957 --> 00:43:09.292
What's causing this spike?

00:43:09.501 --> 00:43:10.460
Die!

00:43:10.668 --> 00:43:12.712
Die! Die!

00:43:12.921 --> 00:43:15.006
The Ashra Force won't be beaten
by the likes of you!

00:43:15.215 --> 00:43:16.716
Die!

00:43:26.643 --> 00:43:28.144
Die!

00:43:40.198 --> 00:43:41.699
Die!

00:44:01.678 --> 00:44:03.513
Are these things real ghosts?

00:44:05.181 --> 00:44:06.683
Die!

00:44:08.059 --> 00:44:10.979
Check the values of all pilots'
neuro devices, Kate!

00:44:11.187 --> 00:44:16.025
There's a signal backflow in Sayama,
Kosaka, and Naruse's neuro devices!

00:44:17.527 --> 00:44:21.698
The brainwaves of all four have
begun to sync. They're networked?

00:44:21.906 --> 00:44:23.408
Die!

00:44:29.706 --> 00:44:31.207
| can see you!

00:44:34.294 --> 00:44:35.795
Die!

00:44:39.215 --> 00:44:40.550
What are these things?!

00:44:40.758 --> 00:44:43.511
Ferilli! Kate! Can you confirm on your end?

00:44:43.720 --> 00:44:45.847
<i>Yes, ma'am! Confirmed! And you?</i>

00:44:46.055 --> 00:44:48.266
No doubt about it! No, wait...

00:44:48.474 --> 00:44:50.518
Doesn't this mean they're syncing with Akito?

00:44:50.727 --> 00:44:51.561
Joe Wise!

00:44:51.769 --> 00:44:53.688
Give me a minute!

00:44:53.897 --> 00:44:56.191
Um, what's going on, Dr. Randle?

00:44:56.399 --> 00:44:57.901
Ask me later!

00:44:59.027 --> 00:45:00.403
Joe Wise, get me data!

00:45:00.612 --> 00:45:02.238
Y-Y
es, ma'am!

00:45:07.660 --> 00:45:10.038
The Ashra Force can't beat
a bunch of Europian pipsqueaks?!

00:45:16.419 --> 00:45:19.130
The Ashra Force's formation is breaking down.

00:45:19.339 --> 00:45:21.382
Facing lowly Europian Knightmares...

00:45:21.591 --> 00:45:22.467
What cowards.

00:45:22.675 --> 00:45:25.678
Jean, you talk too much.

00:45:25.887 --> 00:45:28.014
My apologies, Lord Hyuga.

00:45:29.057 --> 00:45:34.062
Those Knightmares are most interesting.
Do you see what I see, Jean?

00:45:34.270 --> 00:45:36.314
No, I'm not quite...

00:45:38.107 --> 00:45:39.609
| sense it...

00:45:43.112 --> 00:45:45.073
So, you're alive.

00:45:47.283 --> 00:45:48.785
This is bad!

00:45:53.122 --> 00:45:54.666
This guy is dangerous!

00:46:07.512 --> 00:46:10.223
This is not good! Those guys are dangerous!

00:46:10.431 --> 00:46:14.018
It. Hyuga! Please respond! Someone!

00:46:14.227 --> 00:46:17.939
W.O. Kosaka! W.O. Sayama! W.O. Naruse!

00:46:18.147 --> 00:46:20.024
Someone answer me!

00:46:21.693 --> 00:46:23.361
Mental clouding intensifying!

00:46:23.569 --> 00:46:25.989
If this keeps up,
their ego boundaries will break down!

00:46:26.197 --> 00:46:30.159
Akito's nervous system is
co-opting those of Sayama,

00:46:30.368 --> 00:46:35.206
Naruse, and Kosaka via their neuro devices.

00:46:35.415 --> 00:46:37.417
A brain raid!

00:46:47.593 --> 00:46:49.095
I'm taking a pounding!

00:46:51.723 --> 00:46:53.057
Simon, eject!

00:46:53.266 --> 00:46:54.767
Franz!

00:46:56.019 --> 00:46:58.521
We're not about to lose to
inferiors like you people!

00:47:03.109 --> 00:47:04.610
Die!

00:47:07.905 --> 00:47:09.407
Damn monster!

00:47:23.546 --> 00:47:25.048
He's tough...

00:47:26.424 --> 00:47:28.259
You damn angel of death!

00:48:00.541 --> 00:48:02.794
You aren't a ghost!

